{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Tales from the Workplace", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Right Fit", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's backgrounds in a wider variety  of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Using Modals to Add Meaning", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to communicate a precise idea, you can use modal verbs to help you. Modals are verbs or verb phrases that add meaning to the main verb. Depending on which modal you choose, it can add the meaning of advice, strong advice or obligation. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some modals that are often used in the context are:  <span class=\"italic\">should/ought to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>,  and <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> is not used very often in conversation, but you may see it being used in writing. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the following chart with examples of each modal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Should</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When you are applying for work, you  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">should</span> focus your time only on jobs that match your resume perfectly.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Ought to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ought to</span> be discriminating about where you apply.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Had better</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Strong Advice <br/>(Necessity)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had better not</span> \u201cwing it\u201d during an interview.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Supposed to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Obligation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The average person will bring a copy of their resume to an interview, which is what you're  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">supposed to</span> do. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to reduce the sound of  <span class=\"strong\">had</span> in  <span class=\"strong\">had better</span> to  <span class=\"strong\">'d</span>.  <br> For example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">'d better</span> not \"wing it\" in an interview. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Notice the <span class=\"underline\">question form</span>  of these modals: <br> <span class=\"italic\">What should I do before an interview? <br> Ought I to bring a copy of my resume? <br> How had I better dress for an interview? <br> What am I supposed to ask in an interview? </span> ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talking About the Future Using <span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Shall</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">shall</span> to give information about the future or to make predictions (talk about what we think or guess) about the future. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "This is the form you use:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span>/<span class=\"italic\">shall</span> + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">It will be cold tomorrow.<br/>He shall call me next week.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Speakers of North American English rarely use <span class=\"italic\">shall</span> in this way, as it sounds too formal in conversation. It is sometimes used in writing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions for <span class=\"italic\">will</span> (<span class=\"italic\">I'll</span>, <span class=\"italic\">She'll</span>, <span class=\"italic\">He'll</span>, <span class=\"italic\">They'll</span>, <span class=\"italic\">It'll</span>). Practice saying these sentences out loud: <br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I'll </span> step it up a notch. <br><span class=\"strong\"> He'll</span> apply for all the jobs he sees. <br> <span class=\"strong\">They'll </span> be sure to include a cover letter with their resume. <br> <span class=\"strong\">We'll </span> practice the interview a few times. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I hope the advice I have will propel you towards that dream job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This will include your resume, cover letter, reference letters and examples of previous work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Taking the time to research the company and to practice your personal statement shall guarantee a smoother, more relaxed interview.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The average person will bring a copy of their resume to an interview.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "a wealth of experience", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a lot of experience", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cooper Anderson has a wealth of experience I hope you can draw from. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about job hunting.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to work your way up the chain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to start from a low position and work hard to get to a high position", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As the CEO of Cambridge Life magazine, I've worked my way up the chain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to propel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to push forward", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope the advice I have will propel you towards that dream job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to trump", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be better than something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Quality trumps quantity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to personalize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "change something or \u200badd to it so that it is \u200bobvious that it \u200bcomes from you", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You ought to be discriminating about where you apply and focus your energy on writing personalized cover letters.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to step it up a notch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "do a bit more; work a little harder", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why not step it up a notch and bring a portfolio folder?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "portfolio", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a collection of work like photographs or writing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should bring a portfolio of your photos to the interview.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to wing it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to try to do something without preparing first", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You had better not \u201cwing it\u201d during an interview.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you are going to interview an expert at job hunting for the radio.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, write the dialogue for the interview.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the interview with your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Perform the interview in front of your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about jobs, work, manners and customs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I should, ought to, had better or am supposed to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about future action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write an interview dialogue.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about jobs, work, manners and customs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I should, ought to, had better, or am supposed to do.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk abou