estion"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 11, "type": "RSLT"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar", "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le06ob07re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le06ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le06ob07re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le06ob07re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p>Dear Readers,\nMy last article about job hunting tips was received very well! I decided to invite a guest blogger, Cooper Anderson, who has a wealth of experience I hope you can draw from. </p>"}, {"time": "11000", "image": "engenn9le06ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p>As the CEO of Cambridge Life magazine, I've worked my way up the chain, so to speak. I've applied for, interviewed for and landed (most of the time) a variety of different jobs. I hope the advice I have will propel you towards that dream job.</p>\n<ol start=\"1\"><li>Quality trumps quantity</li></ol>\nWhen you are applying for work, you should focus your time and effort only on jobs that match your resume perfectly. Applying for 200 jobs that \u201csort of\u201d suit your skills is a waste of time.\nYou ought to be discriminating about where you apply and focus your energy on writing personalized cover letters."}, {"time": "45000", "image": "engenn9le06ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<ol start=\"2\"><li>Impress with a portfolio</li></ol>\nThe average person will bring a copy of their resume to an interview, which is what you're supposed to do. Why not step it up a notch and bring a portfolio folder? This will include your resume, cover letter, reference letters and examples of previous work.\n<ol start=\"3\"><li>Practice makes perfect</li></ol>\nYou had better not \u201cwing it\u201d during an interview. It is best to be prepared for any type of question they may throw at you. Taking the time to research the company and to practice your personal statement shall guarantee a smoother, more relaxed interview."}]}}], "_data": [], "id": 1, "type": "audio"}]}], "type": "sena"}